==German==

===Etymology===
{{root|de|ine-pro|*weyd-}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|-}} and {{inh|de|goh|wizzan}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*witan}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*witaną}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*wóyde|t=to see, to know}}.

Compare {{cog|nl|weten}}, {{cog|da|vide}}, {{cog|sv|veta}}, archaic Modern {{cog|en|wit}} and {{cog|la|videō|t=to see}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈvɪsn̩/|/ˈvɪsən/}}
* {{audio|de|De-wissen.ogg}}
* {{audio|de|DE-wissen.ogg}}
* {{audio|de|BY-wissen.ogg|a=Bavaria}}
* {{hyph|de|wis|sen}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|wissen<pretpres.weiß#wusste,gewusst,wüsste>}}

# {{lb|de|transitive|or|intransitive}} to [[know]]; to be [[aware]] of (a fact)
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''weiß''', wo du bist.|I know where you are.}}
#: {{uxi|de|von etwas '''wissen'''|to know about something}}
# to [[remember]] {{q|with {{m|de|noch}}}}
#* {{quote-text|de|year=1960|author=w:Marie Luise Kaschnitz|title=Schneeschmelze
|passage=»Als er neun Jahre alt war«, sagte die Frau, »hat er mich zum ersten Mal geschlagen. '''Weißt''' du noch?«|t="When he was nine," said the woman, "he hit me for the first time. Do you remember?"}}

====Usage notes====
* See {{m|de|kennen}} for the distinction between this verb and ''wissen.''

